00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:36.740
Another day in Kamogawa

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:36.740
Another day in Kamogawa

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.090
Is it just me, or are things getting worse?

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:56.550
Yes, that anomaly is gradually descending upon us.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.770
We're receiving similar reports from around the world.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.690
If this continues, Earth will be...

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.400
What's the status of the three pilots?

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.150
Still unable to confirm their location on any of our sensors.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.160
I'm starting to understand

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:22.620
how those guys felt

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.410
when they chose to abandon Earth 20,000 years ago.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.420
Hey! Look at that!

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:32.880
It's getting worse!

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.010
Aren't you afraid?

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.260
I am afraid,

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.220
but I have just as much faith in Madoka.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.980
This may sound funny coming from a relative of hers,

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.270
but she's never let us down, not once.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:56.730
When I want something to happen...

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:04.030
She always finds a way to come through, no matter how serious she needs to become to do it.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:10.120
She'll fly to heights I can't even imagine.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.460
I can't stand this!

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:17.760
I have to do something!

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.470
Where are you going?!

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.260
Where?!

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.720
I don't know!

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.550
The only thing we can do is to wait!

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.810
We have to trust Madoka and the others, and wait.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.140
Against the Vox,

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.900
we're so... powerless!

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.030
Oh, here you are.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.910
Is he still asleep?

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.160
Boss... What are you doing here?!

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.330
I came by to bring Madoka her lunch.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.880
So, are you guys okay?

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.170
Y-Yes, we managed to escape.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:03:59.800
I see.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.130
I'm glad.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.930
Well, you guys can lend me a hand.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:24.990
What do you think happened to your brother, Lan?

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:26.990
I don't know.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.990
<i>Does this mean he was able to get back to the outside world?</i>

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.250
Oh look!

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.630
Brother?!

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.630
The person next to him, is that...?

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.010
It's Yurikano!

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:51.850
Brother!

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.640
Brother!

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:11.990
Hey...

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:13.660
The sound of the waves...

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:14.290
Yeah...

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.250
It's gone?

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.090
This space we call the Rin-ne is connected

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.840
to the hearts of those with a Memoria.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:27.470
Your will has changed this place.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:28.590
In other words...

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.890
The three of you have changed that man's heart.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.280
Please go.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.190
This place will close up soon.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.820
What about you, Yurikano?

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:50.410
I'm staying here with him.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.330
What?

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.160
Don't get me wrong.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.200
I'm not doing this because I love him or anything.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:59.250
Many lives were lost because of us, and I must atone for that.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.130
I'm sure he feels the same way.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.840
No, you can't do that.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:07.760
If you really want to make up for your mistakes,

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.970
then you have to start by being honest with your feelings.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.760
Come on, let's go back together.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.060
We'll take Lan's brother with us too.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:19.480
Don't worry!

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.770
Even after we leave here,

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:24.270
the Jersey Club will be there to help you.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:28.780
We're comrades!

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.910
Not bad for something put together on the fly.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.750
Now, let me hear it...

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.960
the continuation of where you left off 20,000 years ago.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.600
Here it comes!

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.000
Cap! Look at this!

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.640
The aurorae are combining into one?!

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:54.740
That noise...

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:57.330
What is it?

00:07:58.450 --> 00:07:59.750
The sound of the waves?

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.080
No, this is...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.870
<i>When I hear a voice that touches my heart,</i>

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:03.870
It can't be!

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:09.670
<i>I'll put on my jersey and give it my best.</i>

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:13.380
<i>The end result alone isn't enough to inspire me.</i>

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:16.470
<i>I leave it up to my heart to decide,</i>

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:14.720
A song?

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:16.470
A song?!

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:17.550
Is this for real?

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:20.220
<i>on whether or not to take on a request.</i>

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.220
It's the Jersey Club Song!

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.440
<i>Move forward! Move Forward!</i>

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.150
<i>Run! Run!</i>

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:28.940
<i>That's the Jersey Club spirit!</i>

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.040
Cap! It's Aura, Lympha and Ignis!

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.410
I have their signals!

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:42.450
Vital signs normal!

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.250
All three pilots are alive!

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:45.370
Where are they?!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.510
Yeah!

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.010
They did it!

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.600
Did we make it back?

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.680
Snap out of it, Lan!

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:07.310
Look below. We made it home, to Kamogawa!

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:08.560
I see.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.150
Then this is...

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.360
Is something the matter?

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:12.530
No.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.900
For a second, I thought this was the ocean on De Metrio.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.930
Lan! What's wrong?

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:42.680
It's my brother! He's...!

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:55.490
Delicious!

00:09:56.190 --> 00:10:00.160
I never thought I could have your Kamogawa soup on board Pharos!

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.070
More!

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.410
It's all gone.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.410
Huh?! But I'm not full yet!

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.870
How much do you plan on eating?

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.870
It's going to be okay.

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.630
Asteria said there's nothing to worry about.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.090
Right.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:21.680
I was also made younger, by about ten years, after returning from the Rin-ne.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.680
I don't know what happened over there,

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.100
but he probably made the same wish as me.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.520
To have a second chance in life

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:34.150
and pick up from where he left off.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:38.400
Big Brother...

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:43.740
The Rin-ne was a very magical place.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.660
If you wish for something strong enough with all your heart,

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:49.620
the Rin-ne can even reverse time itself.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:53.130
That's what happened to Lan's brother.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.500
If you had gone there,

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:58.720
would the same thing have happened to you, Big Brother?

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.760
You know, I didn't change.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:07.020
I thought I would be turned back,

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:11.060
back to the me when I was always with you, but I didn't.

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:15.730
It looks like I love the way I am right now.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:20.700
Which is why...

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.200
I'll be going.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:38.260
Yurikano!

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.890
Hey. I'm back.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:47.310
What?!

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:48.770
Is that all you have to say?!

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:49.810
Yurikano!

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.100
What's the matter with you?!

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:53.600
Why did you leave us like that,

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:55.520
Yurikano?!

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:02.240
Don't ever leave without telling us again, you hear!

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:08.120
When you go, it'll be with the four of us together!

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:14.040
I'm sorry... and... thank you.

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:19.710
We're getting damage reports

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.970
from branch offices around the world.

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:25.430
It looks like our work is just getting started.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.720
Is something the matter?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:28.970
No,

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.140
it's just...

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:33.270
I feel like we've forgotten something very important.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.990
Aaarrrghh!

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:47.700
I can't get that song out of my head!

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.990
Don't tell me that's the voice of the one?

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:52.250
No, it couldn't be!

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:56.750
That casual march can't be the voice!

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.710
It has to be more...

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:02.300
Majestic, yet plaintive, but profound!

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:06.550
Otherwise it's meaningless to name that universe the "Rin-ne"!

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:10.220
That means I made up that legend for nothing!

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:18.310
Oh, forget it.

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:22.110
The Rin-ne isn't gone. And the Vox are still here.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:25.650
I'll simply have to start anew.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:28.410
Now then, bon... appétit...  {timer - be careful with the "Ã©"}

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:50.300
Hello!

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:51.350
Hi!

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:52.010
Welcome!

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:53.890
This is a surprise.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.060
Are you two on vacation?

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.020
I just got off my early shift.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.060
I'm on break since

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:01.270
our Space University is closed for Golden Week.

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:03.780
There's Golden Week in space?

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:05.820
Anyway, since we don't

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:08.610
get much chance to see each other anymore...

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:10.700
We thought we would drop by to give Madoka photos

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:11.990
from our graduation trip.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.870
Huh? Miss Yoko?

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:17.290
Weren't you leaving today?

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:18.160
I am.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:21.330
Are you waiting for Madoka?

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:24.210
I came by because she wanted to ask me something.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.880
That's the ocean on Le Garite.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:32.390
When I called earlier, she said she'd be here today.

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:36.890
It's like Madoka's gotten even busier since she graduated.

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:39.690
She's just like Auntie.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.270
Are you talking about Madoka's mother?

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:46.400
I always wondered why she was always so busy.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:49.530
I could never quite figure her out, despite being her kid brother.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.450
I'll be going now.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.280
I'm starting to feel like I'm wasting my time waiting for her.

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:54.990
Take care.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:56.040
I will.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.660
Where will you be going this time?

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:58.960
Who knows?

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:01.500
Our Chairman is full of curiosity.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.840
She mentioned something about the Bermuda Triangle

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:09.670
holding the key that connects the Rin-ne to the depths of the Earth's oceans.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:11.930
So I'm guessing that's where we'll start.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:20.100
I hope today and tomorrow will be a happy day for me, and for everyone else.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:22.850
Mom...

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:27.070
Whoa! You surprised me!

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:30.030
Weren't you supposed to be leaving today, Big Sis?

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.450
I came all the way here because you said you wanted to ask me something!

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.250
Ow- oww!

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:43.830
So, what did you want to talk about?

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:44.790
You have one minute.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:51.380
You know that time ten years ago,

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.590
when I nearly drowned?

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:56.550
Yeah... What about that?

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:01.350
I remembered why I went into the water that day.

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:03.560
Did I ever tell you?

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:04.940
No.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:10.240
I jumped into the ocean because I wanted to see Mom.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:16.160
Obviously, she wasn't there, and the next thing I knew,

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:17.830
I was drowning.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:22.460
I thought I was going to die, but that's when Midori poked me.

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:28.550
Maybe that was Mom telling me to snap out of it,

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:30.170
and to live.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:32.170
What do you think?

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:35.640
Big Sis?

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:38.300
Believe what you want to believe.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.520
That's the answer.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:44.100
Yeah.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.100
You're right!

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:53.860
Hello?

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:54.900
Oh, the Le Garite...

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:57.030
What?!

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:58.320
Was that today?!

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:01.450
But it's still a week away on Earth!

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:21.390
Why do I have to dress like this?

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:25.020
You certainly can't attend dressed like a cook.

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:28.520
Wait, so you're really going to become a cook?

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:29.730
Now's a good time to ask.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.520
Do you even know how to cook things besides pasta, Izo?

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.860
That fried egg thing you made was delicious.

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:37.530
So simple, yet profound.

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:40.530
You guys are making fun of me, aren't you?!

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.710
Now we're talking!

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.440
I was starting to think that you wouldn't show up.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:15.900
I had a hard time finding Jersey that would fit me.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:19.700
How's everything going for you?

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.830
As you can see, life can't get any better.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:25.080
Huh?

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:25.830
What's that?

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.000
It's the flower

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.880
that bloomed on the ship that left Earth 20,000 years ago,

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:33.210
and has since been cared for by the Le Garite royal family.

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:35.260
You're giving it to me?

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:36.840
To De Metrio.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:40.720
We're not kings anymore, remember?

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:43.970
All the more reason you'll be able

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:45.640
to keep a single flower in bloom, right?

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:48.770
I guess we really are starting over from scratch...

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:55.230
Hello?

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:57.860
Nah, I wasn't trying to skip out or anything.

00:18:57.860 --> 00:18:58.820
I'll be back right away.

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:02.120
That was my new boss.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:04.450
We're the Kamo-Girls' Jersey Club, Kiss Branch.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:06.620
Want to join?

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:11.620
Branch Chief.

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:13.380
Yes, what is it?

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:16.630
Do I really have to call you by that title?

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:19.260
Yeah! After all, Madoka is the captain!

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.760
Do we have to call ourselves the Jersey Club?

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:34.020
<i>We have reports of yet another miracle resulting</i>

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:36.190
<i>from the abnormal meteorological phenomena which took place late last year.</i>

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:40.360
<i>With regard to the Polyhedron 1000-year problem and measures to deal with the impending collision</i>

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:43.070
<i>of Le Garite and De Metrio,</i>

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.990
<i>a detailed study conducted by a committee</i>

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:47.950
<i>noted a large change in the orbits of both planets...</i>

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:51.210
<i>Novumundus Chairman Asteria Lizamarie De Roschefall,</i>

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:57.050
<i>now also the committee's chairman, promised to make public all data.</i>

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:53.710
Hello?

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.750
Three days from now?

00:19:56.750 --> 00:20:01.260
We can't. We're helping with setting up the shopping district for the summer festival.

00:19:57.050 --> 00:20:01.260
<i>And released a statement saying: "It means we're successful!"</i>

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:04.550
May I ask your name again?

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:07.600
And you're the Secretary-General of which United Nations?

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:09.180
Hey Madoka!

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.100
You're going to be late!

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.350
I know!

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:14.480
I'm very sorry, but I have to get going.

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:16.360
Send me an e-mail with the details.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:18.230
I promise we'll be there!

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:33.620
Can't go anywhere in the Polyhedron without this!

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:37.960
I'm going!

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:40.090
You're late, Madoka.

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:42.380
We were getting tired of waiting.

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:44.130
Sorry about that!

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:44.930
Hey!

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.680
Your lunch.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:49.890
Oh, I forgot.

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:52.390
I made lunches for you two as well.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:54.020
Thank you very much.

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.600
Can't do without this.

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:57.360
Bye, Uncle.

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:00.150
We'll be helping out at the Space Fireworks Festival,

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:03.650
and then be at the De Metrio Nursing Home recreation meeting...

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:06.780
Don't forget our visit to the children's home in the Pa-Dros Star System.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:10.240
We also have to attend a clean-up demonstration at the Intergalactic Debris Meeting.

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:11.620
I'll be coming home at...

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.750
I'm not sure, so I'll call you.

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:15.790
Okay, be careful, now.

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.710
Oh, by the way.

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:21.000
Everyone loved the song you girls sang

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.920
at the unveiling of the Tanpopo Children's Park.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:24.260
Woof!

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.010
Roger that!

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:27.800
Success!

